SUMMARY:Painting Flowers Abstractly\, with local artist Alison Press
DESCRIPTION:A perfect spring art class or Mother’s Day weekend outing! \nThis beautiful workshop\, created by Alison\, is designed for creatives of all levels — especially beginners who are ready to explore abstract painting in an approachable\, supportive environment. Whether you’re brand new to painting or have years of experience\, you’ll be gently guided while also encouraged to trust your own creative instincts. \nWorking with acrylic paints\, we’ll explore color\, form\, line\, and value through bold brushstrokes\, thick and thin lines\, and playful\, expressive interpretations of flowers on canvas. The focus will be on painting loosely\, discovering your own abstract style\, and most importantly — enjoying the process. \nDuring class\, Alison will guide you step by step in creating boldly painted flowers using a loose\, abstract approach. We’ll begin with a quick charcoal sketch of a floral bouquet still-life directly on the canvas. This initial sketch is not meant to be detailed or precise — it simply serves as a relaxed starting point to help you begin confidently. \nBy the end of the workshop\, you’ll leave with a vibrant\, one-of-a-kind floral painting — and the confidence that comes from painting freely\, expressively\, and in community.
URL:https://www.riverartsdistrict.com/event/painting-flowers-abstractly-with-local-artist-alison-press/
LOCATION:ArtPlay Studio\, 53 Orange Street\, Asheville\, NC\, 28801
CATEGORIES:Classes
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://www.riverartsdistrict.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Screenshot-2026-03-16-at-3.00.28-PM.png
ORGANIZER;CN="ArtPlay Studio":MAILTO:info@artplaystudio.com
GEO:35.5807036;-82.5639429
