SUMMARY:Ochre Rose Gallery and Studios Opening Celebration
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a celebration as three fine art painters return to the River Arts District and unite in the historic Cotton Mill. Elizabeth Porritt Carrington\, an Eco-contemplative painter from Ireland is known for her flower filled and portal paintings. Kelcey Loomer creates colorful oil paintings and drawings that reflect her passion for storytelling and narrative images. Amanda McLenon\, a wildlife artist with a background in biology\, is showing her large scale bird paintings with gold and silver leaf. Together\, they have transformed the former Guitar Bar space into Ochre Rose Gallery and Studios. \n“We are excited to invite you into this beautiful warm space to see the threads of connection between our bodies of work. Come by\, help us celebrate this fresh start\, and have a cup of tea or a glass of wine while you spend some time experiencing the paintings. “ Ochre Rose will also serve as a hub for connection and community\, classes and workshops in the future.\nSaturday\, May 16th; we will open our doors for a celebration with light refreshments from 4:00-7:00 pm.\nOchre Rose Gallery\, Cotton Mill\, 122 Riverside Dr.\, Asheville\, NC 28801
URL:https://www.riverartsdistrict.com/event/ochre-rose-gallery-and-studios-opening-celebration/
LOCATION:Cotton Mill Studios\, 122 Riverside Drive\, Asheville\, 28801
